{"bullets":["The oceans cover more than 70% of the Earth's surface and play a vital role in regulating the planet's climate.","They are home to an immense diversity of life, from microscopic organisms to the largest animals on Earth.","Oceans influence weather patterns, contribute to the water cycle, and serve as a major source of food and livelihood for billions of people.","Climate change and pollution are posing significant threats to ocean health.","Ongoing research aims to understand and protect these vital ecosystems for future generations."],"status":"written","title":"Oceans"}